---
// Mount point for lesson 7's controller cascade. The intro screen is rendered
// here rather than in JavaScript, so the lesson still says something without
// it and the opening copy lives in one place. Everything after the start button
// is built at runtime by src/scripts/courses/cascade/cascade.ts.
//
// Nothing is held back. Lesson 7 explains the loop before this runs, so the
// panel is somewhere to try the idea rather than somewhere to derive it, and no
// prose below it is spoiled by reading ahead.
import "@styles/cascade.css";
---

<div data-cascade>
  <div class="cs not-prose my-8">
    <div data-cs-stage>
      <div class="cs-shell">
        <div class="cs-intro">
          <p>
            Five loops, one cluster, and one Deployment asking for three copies.
            Run them, then break something and watch which loop notices.
          </p>
          <div class="cs-foot">
            <button type="button" class="cs-btn" data-tone="primary" data-go="start"
              >Open the cluster</button
            >
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <noscript>
      <p class="cs-note mt-3">
        This panel needs JavaScript. The short version: each loop below watches
        one kind of object, does at most one thing per pass, and never calls
        another loop. A Deployment produces a ReplicaSet, which produces pods,
        which get a node, which get started. Every step happens because something
        read the step above it.
      </p>
    </noscript>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
  import "@scripts/courses/cascade/cascade";
</script>
